Third-party materials and reverse-engineering notice
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is an independent, unofficial, clean-room reconstruction of a
configuration feature for the Fantech Helios II XD3v3 gaming mouse. It is NOT
affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Fantech / Compx. "Fantech",
"Helios", and "XD3v3" are trademarks of their respective owners and are used
here solely to identify the compatible hardware.

No vendor firmware, executable, DLL, image, or source code is distributed in
this repository. Findings were derived by static inspection of a legally
obtained Windows installer and from user-supplied USB packet captures, and are
documented in docs/EVIDENCE.md, docs/PROTOCOL.md and docs/HARDWARE.md.

The USBPcap captures under captures/ are user-supplied evidence and are NOT
redistributed (excluded by .gitignore). Re-record your own captures with the
official Windows software if you need to reproduce the analysis; see
docs/CAPTURE_GUIDE.md.

The protocol constants (report framing, checksum, command IDs, flash map,
startup password words, LED palette, button layout) were recovered from those
sources. They are facts about wire behaviour, not copied code. Any
misstatement is ours alone.

Reference / prior art (studied, not copied):
  * GuessWhatBBQ/FantechX9ThorDriver  - GPL-3.0, userspace Fantech config driver
  * brunobmello25/fantech-driver      - USB capture / protocol analysis workflow

